    "response": "**The Climate Pledge** is a collaborative initiative designed to accelerate global efforts toward sustainability and climate action. Co-founded by Amazon in 2019, it serves as a framework for companies to collectively combat climate change through shared commitments and industry-wide decarbonization.\n\n### Core Definition and Goals\nThe pledge is explicitly defined as <mark>a commitment to reach net-zero carbon emissions across our global operations by 2040</mark> [^1:doc-5501c9cdfc7b318b264a674230dfa432-chunk-000]. \n\nIts broader mission is to <mark>bring together companies from around the world to drive collective action, cross-sector collaboration, and engagement in initiatives that encourage industry action toward decarbonization</mark> [^1:doc-5501c9cdfc7b318b264a674230dfa432-chunk-000].\n\n### Signatory Commitments\nTo participate in The Climate Pledge, companies must adhere to strict sustainability standards. <mark>Signatories commit to regular GHG reporting, making operational changes to decarbonize their business, and neutralizing remaining emissions with credible offsets</mark> [^1:doc-5501c9cdfc7b318b264a674230dfa432-chunk-000].\n\n### Growth and Strategic Focus\nThe initiative has seen rapid growth since its inception. By the end of 2024, The Climate Pledge had expanded to include **549 companies** across **46 countries** and **60 different industries** [^1:doc-5501c9cdfc7b318b264a674230dfa432-chunk-000]. \n\nWith this significant expansion, the focus of the pledge shifted in 2024 toward <mark>working on joint action, small working groups, and addressing shared industry challenges</mark> [^1:doc-5501c9cdfc7b318b264a674230dfa432-chunk-000]. This includes initiatives like the **Science Club Cohort**, which is dedicated to solving measurement challenges in sustainability, as well as supporting six new joint action projects to help signatories navigate common industry hurdles.\n\n### References\n- [1:doc-5501c9cdfc7b318b264a674230dfa432-chunk-000] 2024-amazon-sustainability-report_p16.pdf",
